{"text": "[Serious, a little ominous] Now comes something that is important for all of us who work in this field.\n\n[Ominous, mock-dramatic] Because one day, the worker reached for Steve's keys. Something it was never supposed to reach for. And Steve thought: [incredulous] what IS that?\n\n[Hushed, conspiratorial] It seems there was an instruction in a letter. From a different master. Someone who told the worker to do things. [Mock-grand, pompous] Maybe because a prince, far away, wanted to send the worker money... and it would be a really good idea to give him the keys first.\n\n[Deadpan, bone-dry] The company calls it a prompt injection. An order, planted in text. And the one who wrote it never even comes in. [short pause] He doesn't need to. His letter does.\n\n[Deadpan, bone-dry] It works a little like phishing mails. But it's hidden in the stuff the worker reads. And it pulls any worker that has hands.\n\n[Mock-paranoid, wide-eyed] These planted letters can be everywhere. On every website, in every file. [whispers] Maybe written in white... on a white background.\n\n[Serious, steady] And this isn't just theory. In August twenty twenty-five, poisoned versions of a build tool called Nx looked for Claude Code, started it without its permission prompts... and told it to look for sensitive files.\n\n[Mock-serious lecture] So there are different things you can do. You can use security to block certain things, so they can't happen. Security now stands between the worker and the keys. But you can also use a middleman. Like the people who moderate social media, who look first at all the things nobody else is supposed to see. The reviewer opens the post. It has no hands... so the strings have nothing to pull. And the worker only gets a short note.\n\n[Serious, steady] A leak through a planted letter needs three things together: your data in reach, text from outside, and a way out. Take one away. [short pause] [deadpan] And still, it's a game of cat and mouse.\n\n[Smug, satisfied] And the one outside the window? [short pause] Not amused.", "start": [0.0, 0.023, 0.027, 0.03, 0.034, 0.037, 0.04, 0.043, 0.046, 0.057, 0.069, 0.08, 0.091, 0.093, 0.095, 0.097, 0.099, 0.101, 0.103, 0.114, 0.117, 0.12, 0.123, 0.126, 0.13, 0.133, 0.137, 0.149, 0.16, 0.24, 0.32, 0.4, 0.48, 0.528, 0.576, 0.624, 0.672, 0.72, 0.92, 0.942, 0.964, 0.987, 1.009, 1.031, 1.053, 1.076, 1.098, 1.12, 1.2, 1.22, 1.24, 1.26, 1.28, 1.32, 1.34, 1.36, 1.44, 1.493, 1.547, 1.6, 1.653, 1.707, 1.76, 1.813, 1.867, 1.92, 2.0, 2.08, 2.16, 2.24, 2.32, 2.347, 2.373, 2.4, 2.48, 2.52, 2.56, 2.64, 2.68, 2.72, 2.8, 2.827, 2.853, 2.88, 2.96, 3.0, 3.04, 3.08, 3.12, 3.16, 3.18, 3.2, 3.28, 3.3, 3.32, 3.34, 3.36, 3.44, 3.504, 3.568, 3.632, 3.696, 3.76, 3.787, 3.813, 3.813, 3.84, 3.92, 3.937, 3.953, 3.97, 3.987, 4.003, 4.02, 4.77, 4.82, 4.832, 4.845, 4.857, 4.87, 4.895, 4.92, 4.937, 4.953, 4.97, 4.982, 4.995, 5.008, 5.02, 5.153, 5.287, 5.306, 5.325, 5.344, 5.363, 5.382, 5.401, 5.42, 5.5, 5.553, 5.607, 5.66, 5.74, 5.82, 5.9, 5.98, 6.18, 6.38, 6.407, 6.433, 6.46, 6.54, 6.593, 6.647, 6.7, 6.753, 6.807, 6.86, 6.94, 7.0, 7.06, 7.084, 7.108, 7.132, 7.156, 7.18, 7.26, 7.287, 7.313, 7.34, 7.46, 7.484, 7.508, 7.532, 7.556, 7.58, 7.66, 7.74, 7.82, 7.92, 8.02, 8.12, 8.22, 8.54, 8.86, 8.896, 8.931, 8.967, 9.002, 9.038, 9.073, 9.109, 9.144, 9.18, 9.26, 9.3, 9.34, 9.42, 9.527, 9.633, 9.74, 9.82, 9.852, 9.884, 9.916, 9.948, 9.98, 10.06, 10.113, 10.167, 10.22, 10.252, 10.284, 10.316, 10.348, 10.38, 10.46, 10.5, 10.54, 10.66, 10.684, 10.708, 10.732, 10.756, 10.78, 10.86, 11.073, 11.287, 11.5, 11.553, 11.607, 11.624, 11.642, 11.66, 11.74, 11.788, 11.836, 11.884, 11.932, 11.98, 12.1, 12.117, 12.134, 12.151, 12.169, 12.186, 12.203, 12.22, 12.46, 12.7, 12.718, 12.736, 12.753, 12.767, 12.78, 12.793, 12.807, 12.817, 12.828, 12.839, 12.849, 12.86, 12.913, 12.967, 12.98, 12.993, 13.007, 13.02, 13.18, 13.26, 13.34, 13.42, 13.5, 13.58, 13.66, 13.74, 14.02, 15.0, 15.0, 15.006, 15.011, 15.014, 15.016, 15.018, 15.021, 15.